The bootstrap Requirement is deliberately free of outside concepts. This bean asks which open standards a harness could MAP it to or from, in a layer above bootstrap, and at what cost.

## Done when
- [ ] a survey of open requirements standards and notations (interchange formats, statement templates, quality models), each with licence, maturity and fit to the bootstrap fields
- [ ] a recommendation: which to map in which layer, and whether the markdown front-matter format should change
- [ ] nothing adopted into bootstrap — any mapping lives above it, per the no-outside-concept rule
